# The sync server is meant to be self-hosted (see server/README.md): it is a
# long-running Express process with a SQLite file on a mounted volume. Vercel
# runs serverless functions on a read-only filesystem with no persistent disk,
# so deploying it here would crash on start and could not store backups anyway.
# Excluding it leaves the serverless function in api/ as the only backend.
server/

# Tests. They run locally and in CI, not in the deployment.
test/

# Design-canvas scratch files, not needed by the app.
.thumbnail
uploads/

# Never ship an environment file, even by accident. The template is harmless
# but there is no reason for it to be in the bundle either.
.env
.env.*
.env.example

# Neon's own tooling: neon.ts declares services on Neon's platform and
# hello.ts is a function deployed THERE, not here. Money Manager's backend is
# api/index.js on Vercel; Neon only provides the Postgres database. Excluding
# these keeps the bundle minimal and leaves no root-level .ts for Vercel's
# build step to form an opinion about.
neon.ts
hello.ts
.neon/
skills-lock.json

# Skill documentation for coding agents — not part of the running app.
.claude/
